// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-11-03 (Tuesday) — Carnatic melakarta math
// Melakarta #8: Hanumatodi
// ============================================================================
//
// THE NUMBERING SYSTEM (same chakra/position scheme used every Tuesday this
// project has run — 08-25's #22, 09-01's #20, 09-08's #57, 09-15's #29,
// 09-22's #23, 09-29's #21, 10-06's #65, 10-13's #15, 10-20's #9, 10-27's
// #28):
//   chakra = ceil(N / 6), position = N - 6*(chakra - 1)
// For N = 8: chakra = ceil(8/6) = 2 -> chakra <= 6 means SHUDDHA Ma (M1).
//            Ri-Ga combo index = chakra = #2 of the 6-combo cycle (1=R1G1
//            2=R1G2 3=R1G3 4=R2G2 5=R2G3 6=R3G3) -> R1 G2 (shuddha Ri,
//            sadharana Ga)
//            position = 8 - 6*1 = 2 -> Dha-Ni combo #2 of its own 6-combo
//            cycle (1=D1N1 2=D1N2 3=D1N3 4=D2N2 5=D2N3 6=D3N3) -> D1 N2
//            (shuddha Dha, kaisiki Ni)
// melakarta 8 = S R1 G2 M1 P D1 N2. Semitones (S=0 R1=1 R2/G1=2 R3/G2=3
// G3=4 M1=5 M2=6 P=7 D1=8 D2/N1=9 D3/N2=10 N3=11): 0 1 3 5 7 8 10 — gap
// pattern H-W-W-W-H-W-W, which is exactly Western PHRYGIAN (1 b2 b3 4 5 b6
// b7), no guessing needed: the gaps match the named mode's own formula
// digit for digit. -> .scale("C:phrygian"), degrees: 0=S 1=R 2=G 3=M 4=P
// 5=D 6=N 7=S'. First melakarta Tuesday to land on phrygian specifically —
// 09-29's Kiravani matched harmonic minor, 09-22's Gourimanohari matched
// melodic minor, 10-06's Kalyani matched lydian, 10-20's Dhenuka matched (of
// all things) the Balinese pelog-adjacent scale, 10-27's Harikambhoji
// matched mixolydian; this is the first one of the seven "sampoorna" family
// (all-shuddha-interval-count melakartas matching a full 7-note Western
// mode) that lands on phrygian. Tonic C — not used by any prior melakarta
// Tuesday (E x2, G x3, A x2, F, B, D so far).
//
// Also worth naming: this exact interval set (0 1 3 5 7 8 10) is also the
// Hindustani Bhairavi THAAT (S r g M P d n, all komal except Ma) — the same
// cross-system coincidence 10-06 (Kalyan/Kalyani) and 10-20 (Dhenuka/
// Balinese) already noted, this time Carnatic landing on a Hindustani thaat
// name rather than an unrelated tradition's scale.
//
// KATAPAYADI VERIFICATION (the real naming-to-number encoding, not a
// substitute scheme): the first two consonants of "HAnumatodi" are H and N.
// Katapayadi consonant table: H -> row 8 (ja/da/ha), N -> row 0 (ña/na).
// Digits in name order: 8, 0 -> REVERSE to get the melakarta number: 08 = 8.
// Matches — and cross-checks against the chakra/position math above: chakra
// 2 is the "Netra" chakra, whose six ragas in order are Senavati(7)
// Hanumatodi(8) Dhenuka(9) Natakapriya(10) Kokilapriya(11) Rupavati(12) —
// #8 is the 2nd of those six, matching position = 2 computed independently
// from N. (Also notable: Dhenuka, 10-20's melakarta, sits right next to
// Hanumatodi in this same Netra chakra — two Tuesdays running into the same
// six-raga family, purely by where the math landed.)
//
// THE MATH DRIVING TODAY'S PATTERN — chakra(2), position(2) and N(8) itself
// all drive parameters this time (a richer use of the index than most prior
// Tuesdays managed, which usually picked two of the three):
//   - position (2) -> lead filter LFO sweep period = 2 cycles. Fresh value
//     — no prior melakarta Tuesday used period=2 (used so far: 11, 10, 5,
//     4, 4, 11, 3, 3, 5).
//   - the melakarta number itself (8) -> delay time = an eighth-note
//     subdivision. Fresh fraction (used so far: 1/12, 1/11, 1/5, 1/3, 1/5,
//     1/3, 1/2, 1/4) and, unlike most prior days, drawn straight from N
//     rather than only from chakra/position.
//   - the katapayadi digit pair here is (8, 0) — a zero digit, same
//     situation 10-20's Dhenuka hit, whose fallback was euclid(chakra, N).
//     That fallback would land HERE on euclid(2, 8) — which would be a
//     literal, numeral-for-numeral collision with 10-27's Harikambhoji
//     accent (chakra 5, N 28, which also fell back to euclid(2, 8)), purely
//     because Hanumatodi's chakra and position both happen to equal 2. So
//     instead of the plain euclid fallback, this one reaches for
//     euclidRot(chakra, N, position) = euclidRot(2, 8, 2) — a Euclidean
//     "necklace" rotation, a device no prior melakarta Tuesday has used,
//     and one that puts all three of today's derived numbers (chakra, N,
//     position) into a single call instead of picking two. Gates a pluck of
//     this raga's own defining color tone (the komal Re / b2, scale degree
//     1) inside the EXISTING drone layer. No new kick/snare/hat layer
//     (MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md's autopilot-percussion lesson).
//
// ARRANGEMENT — a Carnatic alapana-style scale exposition over a tambura
// drone, not a tala-bound kriti, so NO metric kit (same standing call as
// every prior melakarta Tuesday — a real alapana has no drum underneath
// it):
//   drone:  sine (purest waveform, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5), tonic + Pa,
//           register-separated (C2 / G3) rather than stacked in one octave
//           — the same choice 10-20's Dhenuka made, reused deliberately
//           here rather than by default: both ragas share the identical
//           defining tension (a komal Re sitting a bare half-step above the
//           tonic), and keeping tonic and fifth apart in register is what
//           leaves that half-step room to read clearly when the accent
//           pluck visits it, the same reasoning that applied there.
//   lead:   sawtooth (synth-basic, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §2.5) — not square
//           (10-20, 09-08) or triangle (10-27, 09-15): phrygian's b2/b3/b6/
//           b7 stack is the starkest, most unambiguously minor color this
//           series has used yet (no major-scale-family degree survives
//           except Sa/Ma/Pa) — sawtooth's full harmonic buzz matches that
//           bare, austere character better than a softer waveform would.
//
// MELODY — four phrases (call / climax-response / drop / motif-variation),
// anchored on S and P, built around the half-step color tone (degree 1):
//   A (call): tonic, leap a fifth to Pa, step down to Ma, leap down a third
//     into the color tone (degree 1) and hang there unresolved:
//                                          0 ~ 4 3 ~ 1 ~ ~
//   B (climax/response, call-and-response device): from the octave above,
//     step down to Ni, leap down through Ga, rest, resolve down to the SAME
//     color tone A ended on — answering A's register with A's own landing
//     point:
//                                          7 6 ~ 2 ~ 1 ~ ~
//   C (the drop, tension->release device): Dha leapt down a fourth to the
//     color tone, rest, then the tonic approached from BELOW (degree -1)
//     resolving up into S — the same "-1 -> 0" idiom this series keeps
//     returning to, here following through with a forward leap up to Pa
//     instead of settling, so the release still points onward into D:
//                                          5 ~ 1 ~ -1 0 4 ~
//   D (motif-and-variation of A — the same opening fifth-leap-then-step, but
//     resolved this time with a firm stepwise descent all the way home to
//     the tonic instead of hanging on the color tone):
//                                          0 ~ 4 3 2 1 0 ~
//
// CYCLES = 28. setcpm(84) -> 28 * 60/84 = 20.0s exactly, seven clean passes
// of the 4-phrase rotation. No tala implied (no drum layer to check a genre
// BPM against) — cpm here just paces the phrase slots for legibility.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(84)
let CYCLES = 28 // 28 * 60/84 = 20.0s; seven clean passes of the 4-phrase melody

stack(
  // DRONE — tambura convention (MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §3): tonic + Pa,
  // register-separated (C2 / G3) rather than same-octave (see ARRANGEMENT
  // above). Plain sine, slow attack/release so it swells rather than snaps.
  note("<c2 g3>/4")
    .sound("sine")
    .gain(.27)
    .attack(2.5).release(3.1)
    .room(4.5),

  // DRONE ACCENT — the raga's own defining color tone (komal Re / b2), one
  // octave up, plucked wherever euclidRot(chakra, N, position) =
  // euclidRot(2, 8, 2) says. Same patch as the main drone, same layer's job
  // (tambura), just the outlet for today's derived numbers instead of a
  // drum hit.
  note("d4")
    .sound("sine")
    .euclidRot(2, 8, 2)
    .gain(.16)
    .attack(.01).decay(.2).release(1.2)
    .room(4.5),

  // MELODY — see MELODY note above. Real leaps (a fifth, thirds, a fourth),
  // rests, call-and-response (A/B share the color-tone landing point),
  // tension->release (C), and motif-and-variation (D vs A) as the required
  // jazz-improv devices.
  n(`<
    0 ~ 4 3 ~ 1 ~ ~
    7 6 ~ 2 ~ 1 ~ ~
    5 ~ 1 ~ -1 0 4 ~
    0 ~ 4 3 2 1 0 ~
  >`)
    .scale("C:phrygian")
    .sound("sawtooth")
    .attack(.007).decay(.11).sustain(.16).release(.18)
    .lpf(sine.range(550, 2600).slow(2)) // position (2) -> sweep period
    .lpq(5)
    .sometimes(x => x.ply(2)) // improv hook: occasional stuttered ornament
    .gain(.45)
    .room(2.5)
    .delay(.22)
    .delaytime(1/8) // melakarta number (8) -> an eighth-note delay
    .delayfeedback(.25)
)
